1. Installer‑Provisioned Infrastructure (IPI)
What it is
IPI is the most automated OpenShift installation method.
The OpenShift installer creates, configures, and manages the underlying infrastructure along with the cluster.


How it works
	• You provide cloud or virtualization credentials
	• Run openshift-install create cluster
	• Installer provisions: 
		○ Compute instances (masters/workers)
		○ Network, load balancers
		○ Storage (where supported)
		○ OpenShift cluster itself

